### Key Factors in Pillar A

**A.1.1 Professional Qualifications**: Addresses formal education, certifications, and professional credentials that establish expertise. Requires documented educational background, relevant professional certifications, industry-specific qualifications, and ongoing professional development demonstration.

**A.1.2 Industry Experience**: Evaluates practical experience and professional track record in relevant fields. Requires documented work history, project portfolio demonstration, client testimonials or case studies, and measurable professional achievements.

**A.1.3 Published Work & Recognition**: Addresses published content, research, and professional recognition. Requires peer-reviewed publications, industry articles, speaking engagements, and professional awards or recognition.

**A.2.1 Institutional Affiliations**: Evaluates connections to credible organizations and institutions. Requires documented affiliations with reputable organizations, institutional endorsements, professional memberships, and collaborative relationships.

**A.2.2 Organizational Authority**: Addresses the credibility and reputation of associated organizations. Requires organizational credibility assessment, reputation validation, industry standing verification, and authority transfer mechanisms.

**A.3.1 Transparency Indicators**: Evaluates openness and transparency in content and operations. Requires clear author identification, contact information accessibility, methodology disclosure, and conflict of interest declarations.

**A.3.2 Consistency Validation**: Addresses consistency across platforms and time periods. Requires consistent messaging across platforms, regular content updates, accuracy maintenance, and reliable information delivery.

