**M.1.1 Page Load Speed Optimization**: Evaluates technical performance for AI system access. Requires Core Web Vitals in "Good" range (LCP <2.5s, FID <100ms, CLS <0.1), successful AI content retrieval within 5 seconds for 95% of requests, and consistent performance across AI platforms.

**M.1.2 Mobile Responsiveness**: Addresses technical requirements for AI access across device types. Requires full mobile compatibility, responsive design adaptation, mobile performance equivalent to desktop, and successful AI system access across all mobile configurations.

**M.2.1 AI Crawler Optimization**: Addresses specific requirements for AI system crawling and indexing. Requires optimized robots.txt configuration, XML sitemap implementation, crawl budget optimization, and AI-specific crawling accommodation.

**M.3.1 Schema Markup Implementation**: Evaluates structured data implementation for AI understanding. Requires comprehensive schema markup, JSON-LD implementation, structured data validation, and AI-specific markup optimization.

**M.4.1 Content Format Optimization**: Addresses content formatting for AI processing efficiency. Requires clean HTML structure, semantic markup usage, content hierarchy optimization, and AI-friendly formatting standards.

**M.5.1 LLMs.txt Implementation and Compliance**: Addresses implementation of LLMs.txt content accessibility standards. Requires proper LLMs.txt file creation, content consolidation implementation, accessibility protocol compliance, and AI processing optimization.

**M.5.2 LLMs-Full.txt Content Consolidation**: Evaluates comprehensive content consolidation for AI accessibility. Requires complete content consolidation, navigation structure optimization, content accessibility enhancement, and AI processing efficiency validation.

